RANK: STATECELL-MARGIN-RQ | position=1 | reason=Only proposal that attacks the measured bottleneck and bounds its own risk: E6/E7 show the gold prefix survives depth 1/2 at 1.000/0.829 but collapses at depth 3/4 (0.161/0.085), so the loss is in the deeper prefix chain, and its capped successor-code margin acts at all three levels; tau_l = median nearest-code squared distance caps behaviour at one typical quantization unit, which is the guard the worst arm l1_br (recall@10 0.04671) lacked; popularity-adjusted p_ij = c_ij/sqrt(1+c_j) answers the E5 top-1-mass skew (0.4375 low-entropy vs 0.0543 high) and the E8 K=256 co-location ceiling 0.0822 (negatives 0.0129); curvature c is derived from the 99th-percentile encoder norm and tau from the data, so no constant is swept, and the three switches plus the 'prefix-match flat => drop' falsifier make a single run decisive.
RANK: succframe-warp-rq | position=2 | reason=Genuine one-pathway coupling — the determinant-one successor-frame warp W_i sits in the nearest-code rule and the level loss at every level, so removing behaviour (B_i=I, s_i=1) or geometry changes the assignment — and it degrades to identity for the many items with fewer than two successors that E5 documents (support 2.77 in the lowest-entropy bin) while adding no new loss constant; but it is a full replacement of the Euclidean residual metric by a warped artanh distance at every level, the exact class E6 shows losing to Euclidean (l1_br 0.04671 and successor_geodesic_coarse 0.05500 against l1_br_euclid 0.06207 and l1_only 0.06233), its stretch clip [1/sqrt d, sqrt d] spans ~32x at d=32 with a real artanh-gradient blow-up risk, and the once-per-epoch frame refresh makes the metric non-stationary against a shared codebook.
RANK: SUCCFRAME-MOEB-RQ | position=3 | reason=Real Mobius coupling (p_l = (p_{l-1} (-) C_l[k_l]) (+) A_l(i) and its exact inverse decode cannot be split into behaviour and geometry), but it also swaps the baseline reconstruction loss for a geodesic loss, so any recall change is confounded between frame and loss and one run cannot separate them — its own risk list concedes this; the frozen rank-d SVD anchor is popularity-driven on a graph E10 puts at 5.45 mean out-degree, and E5 shows most items have under two successors, so it degenerates to plain curved RQ exactly where E6 measures curvature losing (successor_geodesic_coarse 0.05500 vs resample 0.06363); rho=0.5 and tau=0.5493 are chosen defaults, not measured quantities.
RANK: beh-aniso-poincare-rq | position=4 | reason=Structurally correct coupling (the gauge enters the same distance used for assignment and for the tangent Frechet codebook update, with beta=0 / c->0 / both-on switches), but the effect is designed to be tiny: beta in [0,1] bounds the along-successor stretch at sqrt(2), a worst-case cost ratio of 1.41, which against E11's same-first-prefix 0.0907 vs permuted null 0.067 and E8's 0.0822 level-1 co-location ceiling at K=256 is near a no-op; it also replaces the baseline codebook update with tangent Frechet means, discarding the dynamics under which the Euclidean arms reached 0.06207/0.06233, and its own risk list leads with 'anisotropy may be too mild'.
OBJECTION: All four rest on the same weak signal: the OBSERVED evidence caps the behaviour-to-prefix effect at 0.0907 same-first-prefix against a 0.067 permuted null (E11) and 0.0822 behaviour-pair co-location at K=256 against 0.0129 negatives (E8), while the transition graph is thin (115,582 edges, mean out-degree 5.45, 2.72 distinct successors in the low-entropy bin — E10/E5) and no arm in E6 clears the 0.065 target, the best being the non-hyperbolic resample at 0.06363. Because every candidate makes a curved distance the assignment metric, and every curved arm in E6 sits below its Euclidean twin (l1_br 0.04671 vs l1_br_euclid 0.06207; successor_geodesic_coarse 0.05500 vs l1_only 0.06233), even the first-placed proposal carries non-ablatable risk that the geometry term costs the 0.0014-0.005 separating the best observed arm from the target, and with one run, no sweep and no seed repetition that risk cannot be resolved before the round is decided.
